From 84d942254fdc25279499eff153bc75d5b6b9941d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:00:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iOS 10 workqueue, kevent_qos and the system calls its launchd
 needs

- libpthread 218 / libdispatch 703 workqueue: bsdthread_register returns
  the kernel's features and fills in the main thread's QoS; thread
  requests by pthread priority over six QoS buckets; threads get their
  qos_class_t in the upcall flags.
- One event manager thread per process delivers the workq kqueue's
  events (kevent_qos_s, up to 16 per upcall, Mach messages received into
  a 32 KiB area on its stack) and applies the changes libdispatch hands
  back with WQOPS_THREAD_KEVENT_RETURN.
- kevent_qos (374): QoS-sized events, KEVENT_FLAG_WORKQ / IMMEDIATE /
  ERROR_EVENTS, kernel-provided data_out space; EV_UDATA_SPECIFIC knotes.
- EVFILT_MACHPORT on receive rights (not only port sets), receiving
  into the caller's data_out space.
- kqueue_scan_continue passes the caller's data to its callback (it
  passed the uthread scan state, which only kevent's layout tolerated).
- ulock_wait/ulock_wake, bsdthread_ctl, memorystatus_control and
  memorystatus_get_level, coalitions, proc_rlimit_control and other
  no-op controls, the *at() calls, proc_info flavors 17-19,
  csops CS_OPS_IDENTITY, platform-binary status, the
  host_create_mach_voucher trap.
- Mach: ignore EXC_GUARD/EXC_CORPSE_NOTIFY masks, task special ports
  10/11, room for iOS 10's host special ports, and no double release
  of the port on host_set_special_port's error path.
- Diagnostics: exits, reboot reason, unimplemented syscall numbers,
  user prefetch aborts and root image I/O errors go to the serial log.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0123xbco8JF8tibbBMLmXceV
